cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the MICrONS dataset papers listed in the README."
title: "microns-finder: plain-language search of MICrONS cells with Neuroglancer links"
abstract: >-
  microns-finder finds cells in the MICrONS cubic millimeter of mouse visual cortex
  (electron microscopy, CAVE datastack minnie65_public) by cell type, cortical layer,
  visual area and proofreading status, finds synapses between two cell types, and returns
  Neuroglancer links to view them. Cell-type names are mapped to the dataset's label systems
  (AIBS subclass, m-type and multifeature types) with a consensus mode; layers are assigned from
  soma depth with data-derived boundaries. It runs as a Python library, a command-line tool and an
  MCP server, so AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude or Codex can answer plain-language
  requests with real cells.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jsanzros/microns-neuroglancer-finder"
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - MICrONS
  - neuroglancer
  - electron microscopy
  - mouse visual cortex
  - cell types
  - CAVE
  - model context protocol
